"node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "03N4", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "LOCKED_0001": "\\label{section-etale-topology}", "TEXTCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTOPEN_0001": "\\section{"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9e2ace330d512b99c655bc328562f467ff6e7d549c1599871e80c0c0d0269ac2", "source_text": "<TEXTOPEN_0001>The <ACCENT_0001>tale topology<TEXTCLOSE_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:316577534a9ede527cda3a57052a884c25c627eb0b9d97175092cd2210100e92", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:03N4:section_title/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale-cohomology:inventory:etale-cohomology:03N5:definition/0001", "hash": "sha256:9bfd5ab5139d293424a4d7373fbb7a043d32bf46a386de6670bac09bbd081c0a", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 5778, "byte_start": 5487, "file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:1e49eef1a721ad98997a8000dd93b132c8810b39cb4ac1f4eaeae78623146196", "line_end": 155, "line_start": 149}, "owner_tag": "03N5", "parent_tag": "03N4", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03N4", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "LOCKED_0001": "\\label{definition-etale-covering-initial}", "MATH_0001": "$\\{ \\varphi_i : U_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\varphi_i$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$X = \\bigcup_{i \\in I} \\varphi_i(U_i)$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{definition}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{definition}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a65f98beef26737fade1fd89504c8edd78c67195d0d323a6748d8c59c0d868c1", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9191a9fb55f1ea4fb8eb79f5e49555ba1a56cda17fa3fbf5cd7047761c5d7d11", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nA family of morphisms <MATH_0001> is\ncalled an <TEXTITOPEN_0001><ACCENT_0001>tale covering<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if each <MATH_0002> is an <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism\nand their images cover <MATH_0003>, i.e.,\n<MATH_0004>.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7e09414d8517d6b5bf67ea2af6c13798cf8b8fed7992f05d2bbdcad20b544ef8", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:03N5:definition/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale-cohomology:inventory:etale-cohomology:03N4:paragraph/0003", "hash": "sha256:d3c69d93289491a08cd0d45d1c35ba615e69ddbf03ca9fe7d6b72ea2f07c90a4", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 5485, "byte_start": 4646, "file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:25369fe246d5a89bc327bafccf8ac61e64f68bf1b771b61fa81465c181902d05", "line_end": 147, "line_start": 130}, "owner_tag": "03N4", "parent_tag": "03N4", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03N4", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0003": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0004": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0005": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$2$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\Spec(\\mathbf{C}[t])\n\\longrightarrow\n\\Spec(\\mathbf{C}[t]),\n\\quad t \\longmapsto t^2\n$$", "MATH_0003": "$t = 0$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathbf{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$t = 0$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c81c2c39208b8a6912aa0d0e0af5b64c133f3005dfe835219ac172cf6e22779b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6f82b06961197940dc40a0fd22f224678a6d62543be102f4ed045f49d68ace8b", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nA double cover -- loosely defined as a finite degree <MATH_0001> map between varieties\n-- for example\n<MATH_0002>\nwill not be an <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism if it has a fibre consisting of a single point.\nIn the example this happens when <MATH_0003>. For a finite map between varieties\nover <MATH_0004> to be <ACCENT_0002>tale all the fibers should have the same number of\npoints. Removing the point <MATH_0005> from the source of the map in the example\nwill make the morphism <ACCENT_0003>tale. But we can remove other points from the source\nof the morphism also, and the morphism will still be <ACCENT_0004>tale.  To consider the\n<ACCENT_0005>tale topology, we have to look at all such morphisms. Unlike the Zariski\ntopology, these need not be merely open subsets of <MATH_0006>, even though their\nimages always are.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d81c76e15d12b2918e6c9b91984d0c029da9d336f4fb5eea1fa5688d8e74ad72", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:03N4:paragraph/0003"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale-cohomology:inventory:etale-cohomology:03N4:paragraph/0004", "hash": "sha256:b25fe1796486edc8cea1c51063aec304566bbe22dccece7f52e308f29f3bee94", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 5991, "byte_start": 5780, "file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:efad3bc9c63f1e9a82b15fe76b7f63a96292621f9dfcc385bfcaa9d3ed8bc831", "line_end": 160, "line_start": 157}, "owner_tag": "03N4", "parent_tag": "03N4", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03N4", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c7ef4e51c250a7a12b186b1d16bf72c5222d2bdca32e68171a7c6e4320022a77", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7da635d24b69d0e8b6b12b7e5a8d1bbc4941ed30db904268c2b382910256bb8f", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nThis ``defines'' the <ACCENT_0001>tale topology. In other words, we can now say what the\nsheaves are. An <TEXTITOPEN_0001><ACCENT_0002>tale sheaf<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> <MATH_0001> of sets\n(resp.<SPACE_0001>abelian groups, vector spaces, etc) on <MATH_0002> is the data:\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:59b2600dfb31c7192bc5b80a58880abd442d84c55f4b7814b13dd77314f7cb8f", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:03N4:paragraph/0004"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale-cohomology:inventory:etale-cohomology:03N6:remark/0001", "hash": "sha256:77d0e84eb63b7917c323bcd19f612b40886626a9ebe5194243c6a1e7b4979b3f", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 7267, "byte_start": 6995, "file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:c5c41157bd117aaadfb7bc77d44cc51362ab7fb9fe0c356b84958f4db5812da9", "line_end": 193, "line_start": 188}, "owner_tag": "03N6", "parent_tag": "03N4", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "03N4", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{remark-i-is-j}", "MATH_0001": "$i = j$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{remark}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{remark}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9b7ae8363c3756f77a8a90a113b9628e82e08defc628dcee18a6df3239f66420", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:08f449d4cf773e10c709f0b14dd242e1764cd985a2a0438c52deac43796a325e", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nIn the last statement, it is essential not to forget the case where <MATH_0001>\nwhich is in general a highly nontrivial condition (unlike in the Zariski\ntopology). In fact, frequently important coverings have only one element.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:dbc0c0a2efcfe4a77bd884a23d7e9e1d837d41c149f70633ea22d0f2124a0bcd", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:03N6:remark/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale-cohomology:inventory:etale-cohomology:03N4:itemize/0001", "hash": "sha256:47186a9078a8966741e2c319ee76523ac5a2dd101e5a0a45457aca0ce63100eb", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 6993, "byte_start": 6628, "file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:37b7ff3a49884cc1780616eb8a0549d9918493a90bdb391bd1ba4c43c286da96", "line_end": 186, "line_start": 174}, "owner_tag": "03N4", "parent_tag": "03N4", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "itemize", "parent_tag": "03N4", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ITEMCLOSE_0001": "]", "ITEMOPEN_0001": "\\item[", "MATH_0001": "$\\{ \\varphi_i : U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in\nI}$", "MATH_0002": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathcal{F} (U) \\ar[r] &\n\\Pi_{i \\in I} \\mathcal{F} (U_i) \\ar@<1ex>[r] \\ar@<-1ex>[r] &\n\\Pi_{i, j \\in I} \\mathcal{F} (U_i \\times_U U_j)\n}\n$$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{itemize}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{itemize}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:19291a585f59d081f0c682f0f5b8449f120065f8aa1b79d3544998c241acd6c2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d33cdb599489d733239e8dd911323751eaae65f279a51a9890e1a8688b39d2e4", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<ITEMOPEN_0001>(*)<ITEMCLOSE_0001> for every <ACCENT_0001>tale covering <MATH_0001>, the diagram\n<MATH_0002>\nis an equalizer diagram in the category of sets\n(resp.<SPACE_0001>abelian groups, vector spaces, etc).\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0876a35cf43bc85a99a0cb0d1ffc7c1a2e9078f6f7a4b080f529d949af927842", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:03N4:itemize/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale-cohomology:inventory:etale-cohomology:03N4:paragraph/0006", "hash": "sha256:49edecf26cd69b92e48301466c42760104f765c8c69c0389b0e3c5c73c24161f", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 7590, "byte_start": 7269, "file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:82ce7a38c7748742fd3051461ec22a2569c0fa0709d523b5f69eddd3df747fa7", "line_end": 200, "line_start": 195}, "owner_tag": "03N4", "parent_tag": "03N4", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03N4", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:35c639d81a0bc1cae5765cc3a62e799b484cfbe5e82bec7c654fadaba515f4fe", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nSince the identity is an <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism, we can compute the global sections\nof an <ACCENT_0002>tale sheaf, and cohomology will simply be the corresponding\nright-derived functors. In other words, once more theory has been developed and\nstatements have been made precise, there will be no obstacle to defining\ncohomology.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c5eb2d2fdce06481c3288aa1856356c820b9947d970ab17702d431842b8d0ac9", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:03N4:paragraph/0006"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale-cohomology:i